WEBVTT

00:00:49.878 --> 00:00:52.121
Come on, let's say good
night to your brother.

00:00:56.897 --> 00:01:01.153
'Night Sam. Good night, love.

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:04.154
Hey! Dean.

00:01:04.194 --> 00:01:06.503
Daddy! Hey! Buddy.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.336
What do you think? Sam is ready
to touch around football yet?

00:01:09.336 --> 00:01:11.200
No, daddy. No?

00:01:11.247 --> 00:01:12.931
You got him? I got him.

00:01:15.412 --> 00:01:17.126
Sweet dreams, Sammy.

00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:49.482
John?

00:02:10.378 --> 00:02:13.176
John, is he hungry?

00:02:15.314 --> 00:02:16.134
Okay.

00:02:57.719 --> 00:02:59.506
Sammy!

00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:07.734
Mary!

00:03:08.882 --> 00:03:09.702
Mary!

00:03:14.483 --> 00:03:15.245
Mary!

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.214
Hey, Sammy.

00:03:25.948 --> 00:03:27.061
Okay?

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:45.459
Mary!

00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:00.129
Daddy!

00:04:00.222 --> 00:04:01.886
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:04:01.987 --> 00:04:03.300
Don't look back!

00:04:03.486 --> 00:04:04.702
Now, Dean! Go!

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.518
It's okay, Sam.

00:04:32.786 --> 00:04:34.834
I got it. I got it.

00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:39.436
Here.

00:04:55.539 --> 00:04:57.576
Stay back. You have to stay back.

00:05:17.456 --> 00:05:17.886
Sam!

00:05:18.458 --> 00:05:20.155
Get a move on, would ya?

00:05:20.156 --> 00:05:22.261
We were supposed to be
there like 15 minutes ago.

00:05:23.282 --> 00:05:25.041
Sam, you coming or what?

00:05:25.633 --> 00:05:29.322
Do I have to? Yes. It'll be fun.

00:05:30.306 --> 00:05:32.051
And where's your costume?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.059
You know how I feel about Halloween.

00:05:43.515 --> 00:05:46.376
So here's to Sam and his
awesome LSAT* victory.

00:05:46.483 --> 00:05:47.956
All right, all right.
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:47.957 --> 00:05:50.568
Yeah, he acts all humble,
but he scored a 174.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.073
Is that good? Scary good.

00:05:54.115 --> 00:05:56.441
See, there you go. You are
a first-Round draft pick.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.812
You can go to any law school you want.

00:05:58.813 --> 00:06:01.082
Actually, I got an
interview here monday.

00:06:01.551 --> 00:06:04.706
If it goes okay, I think I got
a shot at a full ride next year.

00:06:04.747 --> 00:06:06.636
Hey, it's gonna go great.

00:06:08.048 --> 00:06:08.773
It better.

00:06:08.805 --> 00:06:11.216
How does it feel to be the
golden boy in your family?

00:06:11.222 --> 00:06:12.281
They don't know.

00:06:12.314 --> 00:06:15.111
No? I would be gloating. Why not?

00:06:15.161 --> 00:06:17.185
'Cause we're not exactly the Bradys

00:06:17.237 --> 00:06:19.588
I'm not exactly the
Huxtables. More shots?

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.381
No. No. No. No!

00:06:21.411 --> 00:06:25.460
Seriously, I'm proud of you, and
you're gonna knock them dead on monday.

00:06:25.461 --> 00:06:26.882
You're gonna get that full ride.

00:06:27.245 --> 00:06:28.249
I know it.

00:06:29.086 --> 00:06:30.472
What would I do without you?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.968
Crash and burn.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.957
Whoa! Easy, tiger.

00:07:36.578 --> 00:07:37.383
Dean?

00:07:39.008 --> 00:07:40.471
You scared the crap out of me.

00:07:40.471 --> 00:07:41.921
That's cause you're out of practice.

00:07:44.293 --> 00:07:45.289
Or not.

00:07:45.801 --> 00:07:46.941
Get off of me.

00:07:47.206 --> 00:07:48.975
Dean, what the hell are you doing here?

00:07:49.007 --> 00:07:51.182
I was looking for a beer.

00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:53.536
What the hell are you doing here?

00:07:53.636 --> 00:07:55.341
Ok, all right, we got to talk.

00:07:56.386 --> 00:07:58.900
The phone? If I'd called
would you picked up?

00:07:59.426 --> 00:08:00.263
Sam?

00:08:01.601 --> 00:08:03.667
Jess, hey.

00:08:04.994 --> 00:08:07.002
Dean, this is my girlfriend, Jessica.

00:08:07.726 --> 00:08:09.567
Wait. Your brother Dean?

00:08:09.686 --> 00:08:10.858
I love the Smurfs.

00:08:11.428 --> 00:08:15.173
You know, I got to tell you. You are
completely out of my brother's league.

00:08:15.279 --> 00:08:16.732
Just let me put something on.

00:08:16.779 --> 00:08:20.587
No, no. No, I wouldn't
dream of it, seriously.

00:08:21.623 --> 00:08:24.746
Anyway, I got to borrow your boyfriend here,
talk about some private family business, but

00:08:24.747 --> 00:08:25.938
Nice meeting you.

00:08:27.571 --> 00:08:28.549
No.

00:08:30.485 --> 00:08:32.586
No, whatever you want to say,
you can say it in front of her.

00:08:33.187 --> 00:08:34.190
Okay.

00:08:35.738 --> 00:08:37.723
Dad hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:38.692 --> 00:08:42.986
So? He's working overtime on a "Miller Time"
shift. He'll stumble back in sooner or later.

00:08:44.002 --> 00:08:46.520
Dad's on a hunting trip,

00:08:46.521 --> 00:08:48.942
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:53.874 --> 00:08:55.034
Jess, excuse us.

00:08:56.375 --> 00:08:58.642
We have to go outside.

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:03.555
I mean, come on, you can't just break in the middle
of the night and expect me to hit the road with you.

00:09:03.556 --> 00:09:05.641
You're not hearing me,
Sammy. Dad's missing.

00:09:05.656 --> 00:09:07.465
I need you to help me find him.

00:09:07.253 --> 00:09:10.584
You remember the poltergeist in
Amherst, or the devil's gates in Clifton?

00:09:10.656 --> 00:09:13.997
He was missing then, too. He's
always missing, and he's always fine.

00:09:13.998 --> 00:09:16.359
Not for this long. Now, are
you gonna come with me or not?

00:09:16.676 --> 00:09:17.649
I'm not.

00:09:18.039 --> 00:09:18.756
Why not?

00:09:18.804 --> 00:09:21.106
I swore I was done hunting. For good.

00:09:21.361 --> 00:09:24.118
Come on, it wasn't easy,
but it wasn't that bad. Yeah?

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:27.935
When I told dad I was scared of the
thing in my closet, he gave me a .45.

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:29.067
What was he supposed to do?

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.030
I was 9 years old.

00:09:31.759 --> 00:09:34.030
He was supposed to say:
"Don't be afraid of the dark."

00:09:34.088 --> 00:09:35.678
"Don't be afraid of the
dark"? Are you kidding me?

00:09:35.679 --> 00:09:37.836
Of course, you should be afraid.
You know what's out there.

00:09:37.877 --> 00:09:40.533
Yeah I know but still... The way
we grew up after mom was killed

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:43.096
And dad's obsession to find
the thing that killed her.

00:09:43.141 --> 00:09:45.579
But we still haven't
found the damn thing.

00:09:45.709 --> 00:09:47.255
So we kill everything we can find.

00:09:47.387 --> 00:09:49.689
Save a lot of people doing it, too.

00:09:52.273 --> 00:09:54.026
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:09:56.025 --> 00:09:59.779
The weapon training and
melting the silver into bullets?

00:09:59.856 --> 00:10:02.408
Man, Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:03.475
So, what are you gonna do?

00:10:03.675 --> 00:10:06.419
Are you just gonna live
some normal, apple-Pie life?

00:10:06.036 --> 00:10:07.031
Is that it?

00:10:07.168 --> 00:10:09.487
No, not normal. Safe.

00:10:10.015 --> 00:10:11.772
And that's why you ran away.

00:10:15.182 --> 00:10:16.683
I was just going to college.

00:10:16.684 --> 00:10:19.969
It was dad who said if I was
gonna go, I should stay gone.

00:10:21.492 --> 00:10:22.551
And that's what I'm doing.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:26.513
Dad's in real trouble right now if
he's not dead already. I can feel it.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:30.846
I can't do this alone.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.465
Yes, you can.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.591
Yeah. Well, I don't want to.

00:10:44.037 --> 00:10:45.440
What was he hunting?

00:10:51.343 --> 00:10:54.548
All right. Let's see. Where
the hell did I put that thing?

00:10:54.614 --> 00:10:56.590
So when dad left, why
didn't you go with him?

00:10:56.823 --> 00:11:00.353
I was working my own gig... This
voodoo thing down in New Orleans.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:03.383
Dad let you go on a
hunting trip by yourself?

00:11:03.935 --> 00:11:05.210
I'm 26, dude.

00:11:06.621 --> 00:11:08.350
All right, here we go.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:12.888
So dad was checking out this two-Lane
blacktop just outside of Jericho, California.

00:11:12.987 --> 00:11:14.391
About a month ago, this guy...

00:11:14.656 --> 00:11:17.801
They found his car, but he'd
vanished. Completely M.I.A.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.192
So maybe he was kidnapped.

00:11:20.231 --> 00:11:22.249
Yeah, well, here's another one in April,

00:11:22.393 --> 00:11:27.861
Another one in December '04, '03, '98,
'92... 10 of them over the past 20 years...

00:11:28.156 --> 00:11:30.934
All men, all same
5-Mile stretch of road.

00:11:33.016 --> 00:11:35.103
Started happening more and more, so

00:11:35.136 --> 00:11:36.634
Dad went to go dig around.

00:11:36.656 --> 00:11:38.410
That was about three weeks ago.

00:11:38.815 --> 00:11:41.206
I hadn't heard from him
since, which is bad enough,

00:11:42.446 --> 00:11:44.524
And then I get this
voice mail yesterday.

00:11:45.067 --> 00:11:49.103
<i>Dean, something is starting to
happen. I think it's serious.</i>

00:11:49.191 --> 00:11:51.128
<i>I need to try to figure
out what's going on.</i>

00:11:54.817 --> 00:11:58.078
<i>Be very careful, Dean.
We're all in danger.</i>

00:11:58.746 --> 00:12:00.279
You know there's EVP on that?

00:12:00.377 --> 00:12:03.207
Not bad, Sammy. Kind of
like riding a bike, isn't it?

00:12:03.947 --> 00:12:07.010
All right. I slowed the message
down and ran it through a goldwave,

00:12:07.041 --> 00:12:08.778
Took out the hiss,
and this is what I got.

00:12:10.354 --> 00:12:13.919
<i>I can never go home.</i>

00:12:16.269 --> 00:12:17.865
Never go home.

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:27.538
You know, in almost two years, I've never
bothered you, never asked you for a thing.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.221
All right, I'll go.

00:12:38.129 --> 00:12:39.615
I'll help you find him,

00:12:39.839 --> 00:12:41.748
But I have to get back
first thing Monday.

00:12:42.108 --> 00:12:43.078
Just wait here.

00:12:43.396 --> 00:12:45.132
What's first thing monday?

00:12:46.607 --> 00:12:48.234
I've this...

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:50.742
I have an interview.

00:12:50.758 --> 00:12:52.567
What? A job interview? Skip it.

00:12:54.374 --> 00:12:58.667
It's a law-School interview, and
it's my whole future on a plate.

00:12:58.739 --> 00:12:59.663
Law school?

00:13:00.543 --> 00:13:02.201
So we got a deal or not?

00:13:06.461 --> 00:13:07.979
Wait, you're taking off?

00:13:08.259 --> 00:13:09.730
Is this about your dad? Is he all right?

00:13:09.871 --> 00:13:12.296
Yeah. You know, just
a little family drama.

00:13:12.769 --> 00:13:15.410
But your brother said he was
on some kind of hunting trip.

00:13:15.465 --> 00:13:18.104
Yeah, he's just deer
hunting up at the cabin,

00:13:18.256 --> 00:13:21.503
And he's probably got Jim,
Jack, and Jose along with him.

00:13:21.506 --> 00:13:23.165
We're just gonna go bring him back.

00:13:23.162 --> 00:13:24.257
What about the interview?

00:13:25.048 --> 00:13:26.206
I'll make the interview.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:27.750
This is only for a couple days.

00:13:27.856 --> 00:13:30.572
Sam, I mean, please.
Just stop for a second.

00:13:31.514 --> 00:13:32.594
You're sure you're okay?

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.570
I'm fine

00:13:35.356 --> 00:13:38.689
It's just... You want
even talk about your family

00:13:39.142 --> 00:13:42.148
And now you're taking off the middle of
the night to spend the week-End with them

00:13:42.367 --> 00:13:45.214
And with Monday coming up...
It's just not kind of your style.

00:13:45.259 --> 00:13:47.570
Hey, everything's gonna be okay.

00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:50.508
I would be back in time, I promise.

00:13:54.224 --> 00:13:55.747
At least tell me where you're going!

00:14:05.819 --> 00:14:07.571
Amy, I can't come over tonight.

00:14:08.543 --> 00:14:11.156
Because I got work in
the morning, that's why.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.020
Okay, I miss it, my
dad's gonna have my ass.

00:14:20.634 --> 00:14:22.370
Hey, uh, Amy, let me call you back.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.181
Car trouble or something?

00:14:42.365 --> 00:14:44.399
Take me home.

00:14:45.917 --> 00:14:47.168
Sure, get in.

00:15:03.389 --> 00:15:05.861
So where do you live?

00:15:08.834 --> 00:15:11.400
At the end of Breckenridge Road.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.817
You're coming from a
Halloween party or something?

00:15:19.576 --> 00:15:23.503
You know, um, a girl like you
really shouldn't be alone out here.

00:15:34.813 --> 00:15:36.550
I'm with you.

00:15:48.068 --> 00:15:50.133
Do you think I'm pretty?

00:15:54.936 --> 00:15:56.704
Will you come home with me?

00:15:56.986 --> 00:15:59.770
Um...Hell, yeah.

00:16:19.487 --> 00:16:21.771
Come on. You don't live here.

00:16:23.272 --> 00:16:24.726
I can never go home

00:16:25.086 --> 00:16:29.138
What? What are you talking
about? Nobody lives here.

00:16:29.502 --> 00:16:31.239
Huh, where do you live?

00:16:38.331 --> 00:16:39.974
That's good.

00:16:40.835 --> 00:16:42.290
Joke's over, okay?

00:16:45.652 --> 00:16:47.201
You want me to leave?

00:17:07.028 --> 00:17:07.982
Hello?

00:17:15.421 --> 00:17:16.891
Hello?

00:18:17.627 --> 00:18:19.833
Hey. You want breakfast?

00:18:20.323 --> 00:18:21.434
No, thanks.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:26.315
So how'd you pay for that stuff? You
and dad still running credit-Card scams?

00:18:26.476 --> 00:18:29.762
Yeah, well, hunting ain't
exactly a pro-Ball career.

00:18:31.326 --> 00:18:33.896
Besides, all we do is apply. It's
not our fault they send us the cards.

00:18:33.927 --> 00:18:38.216
Yeah, and what names did you
write on the application this time?

00:18:38.284 --> 00:18:43.935
Uh... Bert Aframian and his son,
Hector. Scored two cards out of the deal.

00:18:44.029 --> 00:18:45.523
Sounds about right.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.643
I swear, man,you got to update
your cassette-Tape collection.

00:18:48.715 --> 00:18:49.435
Why?

00:18:49.576 --> 00:18:51.539
Well, for one... They're cassette tapes.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.540
And two...

00:18:52.541 --> 00:18:56.728
Black Sabbath, Motorhead, Metallica?

00:18:57.095 --> 00:18:59.787
It's the greatest hits of mullet rock.

00:19:00.027 --> 00:19:02.321
House rules, Sammy...
driver picks the music,

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.972
Shotgun shuts his cake hole.

00:19:04.739 --> 00:19:07.368
Yo Sammy is a chubby
12-Year-Old. It's...

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.154
Sorry, I can't hear you.
The music's too loud.

00:19:27.789 --> 00:19:29.001
Thank you.

00:19:30.211 --> 00:19:33.107
All right. So there's no one matching
dad at the hospital or morgue.

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.399
So that's something, I guess.

00:19:37.757 --> 00:19:38.789
Check it out.

00:20:02.488 --> 00:20:03.458
Let's go.

00:20:07.519 --> 00:20:09.272
Did you guys find anything?

00:20:09.303 --> 00:20:11.978
No! Nothing!

00:20:16.865 --> 00:20:20.062
No sign of struggle, no
footprints, no fingerprints...

00:20:20.063 --> 00:20:21.063
Spotless. It's almost too clean.

00:20:21.939 --> 00:20:23.564
So this kid, Troy...

00:20:23.565 --> 00:20:25.563
He's dating your daughter, isn't he? Ya.

00:20:25.564 --> 00:20:26.647
How's Amy doing?

00:20:26.757 --> 00:20:28.806
She's been putting up
missing posters downtown.

00:20:29.901 --> 00:20:32.639
You had another one like
this last month, didn't you?

00:20:33.828 --> 00:20:35.001
And who are you?

00:20:35.549 --> 00:20:36.988
Federal marshals.

00:20:38.526 --> 00:20:40.654
You two are a little young
for marshals, aren't you?

00:20:40.842 --> 00:20:42.500
Thanks, that's awfully kind of you.

00:20:43.068 --> 00:20:44.993
You did have another one
just like this, correct?

00:20:45.149 --> 00:20:45.900
Yeah, that's right,

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:48.419
About a mile up the road. There
have been others before that.

00:20:48.471 --> 00:20:51.178
So this victim... You knew him?

00:20:51.944 --> 00:20:53.931
A town like this,
everybody knows everybody.

00:20:53.994 --> 00:20:56.779
Any connection between the victims
besides that they're all men?

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.748
No. Not so far as we can tell.

00:20:59.108 --> 00:21:00.156
So what's the theory?

00:21:00.286 --> 00:21:01.609
Honestly, we don't know...

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:04.031
Serial murderer, kidnapping ring.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:08.140
Well, that is exactly the kind of crack
police work I'd expect out of you guys.

00:21:08.598 --> 00:21:10.585
Thank you for your time.

00:21:11.054 --> 00:21:12.822
Gentlemen.

00:21:21.313 --> 00:21:22.328
What was that for?

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:24.955
Why do you have to step on my foot? Why
do you have to talk to police like that?

00:21:25.165 --> 00:21:27.574
Come on. They don't really
know what's going on.

00:21:27.682 --> 00:21:28.842
We're all alone on this.

00:21:28.843 --> 00:21:31.931
If we're gonna find dad, we've got to
get to the bottom of this thing ourselves.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:35.996
Can I help you boys?

00:21:36.508 --> 00:21:38.308
No, sir. We were just leaving.

00:21:38.309 --> 00:21:40.604
Agent Mulder, agent Scully.

00:21:48.994 --> 00:21:50.324
I'll bet you that's her.

00:21:50.622 --> 00:21:51.529
Yeah.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:55.221
You must be Amy. Yeah.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:58.574
Troy told us about you. We're his
uncles. I'm Dean. This is Sammy.

00:21:58.809 --> 00:22:00.170
He never mentioned you to me.

00:22:00.749 --> 00:22:01.969
Well, that's Troy, I guess.

00:22:02.016 --> 00:22:03.719
We're not around much.
We're up in Modesto.

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:07.630
So we're looking for him, too,
and we're kind of asking around.

00:22:07.835 --> 00:22:10.025
Hey, are you okay? Yeah.

00:22:10.265 --> 00:22:12.471
Do you mind if we ask
you a couple questions?

00:22:13.524 --> 00:22:16.210
I was on the phone with
Troy. He was driving home.

00:22:16.211 --> 00:22:21.064
He said he would call me
right back, and he never did.

00:22:21.065 --> 00:22:23.620
He didn't say anything
strange? Or out of the ordinary?

00:22:23.766 --> 00:22:26.613
No, nothing I can remember.

00:22:28.057 --> 00:22:29.403
I like your necklace.

00:22:32.145 --> 00:22:33.381
Troy gave it to me.

00:22:34.028 --> 00:22:37.955
Mostly to scare my parents...
You know, the devil stuff.

00:22:40.431 --> 00:22:42.650
Actually it means just the opposite.

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:45.398
A pentagram is a
protection against evil.

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:48.504
Really powerfull, I mean if
you believe in a kind of thing.

00:22:48.649 --> 00:22:50.996
Ok, thank you, Unsolved Mysteries.

00:22:51.246 --> 00:22:52.450
Here's the deal, ladies...

00:22:52.451 --> 00:22:55.954
The way Troy disappeared...
Something's not right.

00:22:55.955 --> 00:22:58.058
So if you've heard anything...

00:23:00.351 --> 00:23:01.259
What is it?

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:02.877
Well, it's just...

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:05.906
I mean, with all these guys
going missing, people talk.

00:23:05.952 --> 00:23:07.141
What do they talk about?

00:23:10.916 --> 00:23:13.028
It's kind of this local legend.

00:23:13.294 --> 00:23:17.925
This one girl, she got murdered
out on Centennial like decades ago.

00:23:18.529 --> 00:23:21.173
Well, supposedly, she's still out there.

00:23:21.569 --> 00:23:24.959
She hitchhikes, and
whoever picks her up...

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:28.132
Well, they disappear forever.

00:23:45.232 --> 00:23:47.062
Let me try. I got it.

00:23:48.423 --> 00:23:49.268
Dude.

00:23:50.785 --> 00:23:52.944
You're such a control freak.

00:23:53.679 --> 00:23:56.667
So angry spirits are born out
of violent death, right? Yeah

00:23:57.043 --> 00:23:58.451
Maybe it's not murder.

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:12.673
This was 1981. Constance Welch, 24 years old,
jumps off Sylvania Bridge, drowns in the river.

00:24:12.704 --> 00:24:14.461
Does it say why she did it? Yeah.

00:24:14.852 --> 00:24:15.415
What?

00:24:16.151 --> 00:24:18.502
An hour before they
found her, she calls 911.

00:24:18.565 --> 00:24:21.716
Her two little kids are in the bathtub.
She leaves them alone for a minute,

00:24:21.717 --> 00:24:22.889
And when she comes back,

00:24:22.961 --> 00:24:24.213
They aren't breathing.

00:24:24.893 --> 00:24:25.910
Both died.

00:24:26.901 --> 00:24:29.488
"Our babies were gone, and
Constance just couldn't bear it,"

00:24:29.489 --> 00:24:30.489
Said husband, Joseph Welch.

00:24:32.867 --> 00:24:34.964
That bridge look familiar to you?

00:24:39.959 --> 00:24:42.963
So this is where Constance
took the swan dive.

00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:45.111
So you think dad would have been here?

00:24:45.893 --> 00:24:48.615
Well, he's chasing the same
story, and we're chasing him.

00:24:50.028 --> 00:24:51.374
Okay, so now what?

00:24:52.359 --> 00:24:54.909
Now we keep digging till we
find him. It might take a while.

00:24:55.107 --> 00:24:58.721
Dean, I told you I've got
to get back by... Monday.

00:24:59.863 --> 00:25:01.631
Right. The interview.

00:25:01.678 --> 00:25:03.258
Yeah. Yeah, I forgot.

00:25:03.921 --> 00:25:05.767
You're really serious
about this, aren't you?

00:25:06.768 --> 00:25:08.974
You think you're just
gonna become some lawyer,

00:25:09.350 --> 00:25:10.601
Marry your girl?

00:25:10.664 --> 00:25:11.806
Maybe. Why not?

00:25:12.014 --> 00:25:15.394
Does Jessica know the truth about you?
Does she know about the things you've done?

00:25:15.597 --> 00:25:17.365
No, and she's not ever going to know.

00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:19.602
Well, that's healthy.

00:25:19.904 --> 00:25:24.425
You can pretend all you want, Sammy, but sooner or
later you're gonna have to face up to who you really are.

00:25:24.852 --> 00:25:25.611
Who is that?

00:25:25.620 --> 00:25:27.117
One of us. No!

00:25:27.246 --> 00:25:29.787
I'm not like you. This is
not going to be my life.

00:25:29.810 --> 00:25:32.878
Well, you have a responsibility. To dad?

00:25:32.206 --> 00:25:33.911
And his crusade?

00:25:34.286 --> 00:25:37.337
If it weren't for pictures, I
wouldn't even know what mom looks like.

00:25:37.732 --> 00:25:39.109
What difference would it make?

00:25:39.359 --> 00:25:41.503
Even if we do find the
thing that killed her,

00:25:42.301 --> 00:25:45.086
Mom's gone, and she isn't coming back.

00:25:51.329 --> 00:25:53.675
Don't talk about her like that.

00:26:02.872 --> 00:26:03.795
Sam.

00:26:16.621 --> 00:26:18.420
Where'd she go? I don't know.

00:26:22.779 --> 00:26:26.424
What the...? Who's driving your car?

00:26:34.108 --> 00:26:36.955
Come on, Dean. Let's go! Go!

00:27:03.356 --> 00:27:04.216
Dean!

00:27:05.637 --> 00:27:06.310
Dean!

00:27:09.134 --> 00:27:09.979
What?!

00:27:13.745 --> 00:27:15.920
Hey, are you all right?

00:27:16.859 --> 00:27:18.032
I'm super.

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:25.054
Car all right?

00:27:25.257 --> 00:27:27.854
Yeah, whatever she did to
it, it seems all right now.

00:27:28.089 --> 00:27:30.233
That Constance chick... What a bitch!

00:27:30.467 --> 00:27:33.236
Well, she doesn't want us
digging around, that's for sure.

00:27:35.197 --> 00:27:37.481
So where's the trail
go from here, genius?

00:27:42.973 --> 00:27:44.553
You smell like a toilet.

00:27:47.565 --> 00:27:48.785
One room, please.

00:27:52.649 --> 00:27:54.543
You guys having a reunion or something?

00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:55.513
What do you mean?

00:27:55.846 --> 00:28:00.273
That other guy, Bert Aframian. He came in
and bought out a room for the whole month.

00:28:30.939 --> 00:28:33.500
I don't think he's been here
for a couple days at least.

00:28:35.664 --> 00:28:38.323
Salt, cat's-Eye shells...

00:28:38.746 --> 00:28:42.506
He was worried, trying to
keep something from coming in.

00:28:45.525 --> 00:28:46.636
What do you got here?

00:28:47.104 --> 00:28:49.717
Centennial Highway victims.

00:28:51.266 --> 00:28:52.596
I don't get it.

00:28:53.159 --> 00:28:57.070
I mean, different men,
different jobs, age, ethnicities.

00:28:57.780 --> 00:28:59.548
There's always a connection, right?

00:29:00.377 --> 00:29:01.801
What do these guys have in common?

00:29:16.930 --> 00:29:18.260
Dad figured it out.

00:29:18.529 --> 00:29:19.781
What do you mean?

00:29:19.829 --> 00:29:21.898
He found the same article we did.

00:29:21.899 --> 00:29:25.313
Constance Welch. She's a woman in white.

00:29:28.288 --> 00:29:29.774
You sly dogs.

00:29:30.071 --> 00:29:33.435
All right, so if we're dealing with a woman in white,
dad would have found the corpse and destroyed it.

00:29:33.623 --> 00:29:35.219
She might have another weakness.

00:29:35.743 --> 00:29:38.270
No, dad would want to
make sure. He'd dig her up.

00:29:38.329 --> 00:29:39.693
Does it say where she's buried?

00:29:40.117 --> 00:29:41.916
No, not that I can tell.

00:29:42.433 --> 00:29:44.639
If I were dad, though,
I'd go ask her husband,

00:29:45.061 --> 00:29:46.313
If he's still alive.

00:29:52.882 --> 00:29:56.027
All right, why don't you see if you can
find an address? I'm gonna get cleaned up.

00:29:56.469 --> 00:30:01.366
Hey, Dean, what I said earlier
about mom and dad... I'm sorry.

00:30:02.195 --> 00:30:03.618
No chick-Flick moments.

00:30:04.797 --> 00:30:06.596
All right... jerk.

00:30:07.738 --> 00:30:08.614
Bitch.

00:30:25.936 --> 00:30:29.362
<i>Hey, it's me. It's about 10:20...</i>

00:30:29.878 --> 00:30:34.077
Hey, man. I'm starving. I'm gonna grab a little
something to eat at that diner down the street.

00:30:34.078 --> 00:30:35.386
You want anything?

00:30:35.693 --> 00:30:36.262
No.

00:30:36.262 --> 00:30:37.559
Aframian's buying.

00:30:55.055 --> 00:30:57.590
<i>So come home soon, okay? I love you.</i>

00:31:00.453 --> 00:31:00.985
What?

00:31:01.224 --> 00:31:02.554
Dude, five-O. Take off.

00:31:03.023 --> 00:31:04.040
What about you?

00:31:04.306 --> 00:31:06.903
Uh, they kind of
spotted me. Go find dad.

00:31:08.875 --> 00:31:10.064
Problem, officers?

00:31:10.236 --> 00:31:11.487
Where's your partner?

00:31:11.736 --> 00:31:13.786
Partner? What? What partner?

00:31:21.227 --> 00:31:24.825
So fake U.S. Marshal, fake credit cards.

00:31:25.091 --> 00:31:26.546
You got anything that's real?

00:31:27.094 --> 00:31:28.001
My boobs.

00:31:29.933 --> 00:31:32.076
You have the right to remain silent.

00:31:34.382 --> 00:31:36.572
So you want to give us your real name?

00:31:36.922 --> 00:31:40.176
I told you. It's Nugent, Ted Nugent.

00:31:42.366 --> 00:31:45.370
I'm not sure you realize just
how much trouble you're in here.

00:31:45.371 --> 00:31:49.724
We're talking, like, misdemeanor kind of
trouble or "squeal like a pig" trouble?

00:31:50.084 --> 00:31:52.838
You got the faces of 10 missing
persons taped to your wall,

00:31:53.250 --> 00:31:56.160
Along with a whole lot
of satanic mumbo jumbo.

00:31:56.535 --> 00:31:58.475
Boy, you are officially a suspect.

00:31:58.637 --> 00:32:02.611
That makes sense 'cause when the
first one went missing in '82, I was 3.

00:32:03.158 --> 00:32:06.068
I know you got partners.
One of them's an older guy.

00:32:06.851 --> 00:32:08.822
Maybe he started the whole thing.

00:32:10.501 --> 00:32:12.707
So tell me, Dean...

00:32:15.106 --> 00:32:16.029
Is this his?

00:32:23.606 --> 00:32:25.108
I thought that might be your name.

00:32:26.735 --> 00:32:28.281
See, I leafed through this,

00:32:28.295 --> 00:32:31.872
What little I could make out. I
mean, it's nine kinds of crazy,

00:32:33.472 --> 00:32:35.193
But I found this, too.

00:32:36.269 --> 00:32:41.964
Now, you're staying right here till you
tell me exactly what the hell that means.

00:32:54.257 --> 00:32:57.386
Hi, uh, are you Joseph Welch? Yeah.

00:32:58.272 --> 00:33:00.013
Yeah, he was older, but that's him.

00:33:00.095 --> 00:33:03.462
He came by three or four days
ago, said he was a reporter.

00:33:03.821 --> 00:33:06.293
That's right. We're
working on a story together.

00:33:07.542 --> 00:33:11.563
Well, I don't know what the hell kind of story
you're working on... the questions he asked me.

00:33:11.641 --> 00:33:13.471
About your late wife, Constance.

00:33:14.441 --> 00:33:16.178
He asked me where she was buried.

00:33:17.028 --> 00:33:18.639
And where is that again?

00:33:19.249 --> 00:33:20.767
What? I got to go through these twice?

00:33:21.064 --> 00:33:23.409
It's fact checking, if you don't mind.

00:33:26.037 --> 00:33:29.448
In a plot behind my old
place over on Breckenridge.

00:33:30.063 --> 00:33:31.612
Why did you move?

00:33:33.035 --> 00:33:36.477
I'm not gonna live in the
house where my children died.

00:33:39.193 --> 00:33:41.274
Mr. Welch, did you ever marry again?

00:33:41.399 --> 00:33:45.013
No way. Constance... She
was the love of my life,

00:33:46.607 --> 00:33:48.438
Prettiest woman I ever known.

00:33:48.657 --> 00:33:50.096
So you had a happy marriage?

00:33:53.613 --> 00:33:54.411
Definitely.

00:33:57.493 --> 00:34:00.215
Well, that should do
it. Thanks for your time.

00:34:10.801 --> 00:34:13.639
Mr. Welch, you ever
hear of a woman in white?

00:34:13.821 --> 00:34:14.556
A what?

00:34:15.025 --> 00:34:18.170
A woman in white or
sometimes a weeping woman.

00:34:19.207 --> 00:34:20.193
It's a ghost story.

00:34:20.416 --> 00:34:23.718
Well, it's more of a phenomenon, really.

00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:27.494
They're spirits. They've been
sighted for hundreds of years,

00:34:27.854 --> 00:34:32.068
Dozens of places in Hawaii and
Mexico, lately in Arizona, Indiana.

00:34:32.109 --> 00:34:33.987
All these are different
women, you understand,

00:34:34.273 --> 00:34:36.150
But all share the same story.

00:34:37.089 --> 00:34:40.254
Boy, I don't care much for nonsense.

00:34:40.411 --> 00:34:41.772
You see, when they were alive,

00:34:42.215 --> 00:34:44.249
Their husbands were unfaithful to them,

00:34:45.156 --> 00:34:46.236
And these women,

00:34:46.596 --> 00:34:49.662
Basically suffering from temporary
insanity, murdered their children.

00:34:51.332 --> 00:34:54.680
Then, once they realized what they
had done, they took their own lives.

00:34:54.977 --> 00:34:56.729
So now their spirits are cursed,

00:34:57.058 --> 00:34:59.076
Walking back roads, waterways,

00:34:59.410 --> 00:35:02.476
And if they find an
unfaithful man, they kill him,

00:35:02.914 --> 00:35:04.651
And that man is never seen again.

00:35:06.294 --> 00:35:07.764
You think...

00:35:08.921 --> 00:35:12.614
You think that has something
to do with Constance,

00:35:13.240 --> 00:35:14.413
You smart ass?

00:35:15.007 --> 00:35:16.149
You tell me.

00:35:19.574 --> 00:35:24.048
I mean, maybe... Maybe
I made some mistakes,

00:35:24.627 --> 00:35:26.301
But no matter what I did,

00:35:26.990 --> 00:35:29.728
Constance never would have
killed her own children.

00:35:31.156 --> 00:35:33.253
Now, you get the hell out of here,

00:35:33.691 --> 00:35:35.302
And you don't come back.

00:35:50.779 --> 00:35:52.750
I don't know how many
times I got to tell you.

00:35:52.969 --> 00:35:54.581
It's my high-School locker combo.

00:35:55.008 --> 00:35:56.698
Are we gonna do this all night long?

00:35:56.776 --> 00:35:59.858
We just got a 911. Shots
fired over at Whiteford Road.

00:36:01.814 --> 00:36:03.331
Do you have to go to the bathroom?

00:36:03.962 --> 00:36:04.604
No.

00:36:04.932 --> 00:36:05.996
Good.

00:36:55.987 --> 00:36:59.179
Fake 911 phone call, Sammy?
That's pretty illegal.

00:36:59.460 --> 00:37:00.227
You're welcome.

00:37:00.321 --> 00:37:01.604
Listen, we got to talk

00:37:01.697 --> 00:37:04.440
Tell me about it. So the
husband was unfaithful.

00:37:04.534 --> 00:37:06.223
We are dealing with a woman in white.

00:37:06.301 --> 00:37:08.874
She's buried behind her old house.

00:37:08.895 --> 00:37:10.095
Sammy, would you shut up for a second?

00:37:10.139 --> 00:37:12.267
I can't figure out why he
hasn't destroyed the corpse yet.

00:37:12.470 --> 00:37:14.911
That's what I'm trying
to tell you. He's gone.

00:37:15.307 --> 00:37:16.386
Dad left Jericho.

00:37:16.433 --> 00:37:18.279
What? How do you know?

00:37:19.093 --> 00:37:19.906
I've got his journal.

00:37:20.094 --> 00:37:21.705
He doesn't go anywhere
without that thing.

00:37:21.898 --> 00:37:22.993
Well, he did this time.

00:37:23.056 --> 00:37:23.807
What's it say?

00:37:23.838 --> 00:37:26.936
Same old ex-Marine crap when he
wants to let us know where he's going.

00:37:26.999 --> 00:37:27.807
Coordinates.

00:37:27.810 --> 00:37:28.810
Where to?

00:37:28.810 --> 00:37:29.977
I'm not sure yet.

00:37:30.002 --> 00:37:34.100
I don't understand. I mean,
what can be so important

00:37:34.101 --> 00:37:35.101
That he just gets out
in the middle of the job?

00:37:34.717 --> 00:37:36.484
Dean, what the hell is going on?

00:37:39.956 --> 00:37:41.348
Sam, Sam!

00:37:47.757 --> 00:37:49.165
Take me home.

00:37:57.135 --> 00:37:59.341
Take me home.

00:38:01.176 --> 00:38:01.958
No.

00:38:42.811 --> 00:38:44.062
Don't do this.

00:38:46.649 --> 00:38:48.260
I can never go home.

00:38:51.300 --> 00:38:53.130
You're scared to go home.

00:39:00.144 --> 00:39:01.224
Hold me.

00:39:02.303 --> 00:39:04.760
I'm so cold.

00:39:05.171 --> 00:39:09.160
You can't kill me. I'm not unfaithful.

00:39:09.395 --> 00:39:11.194
I've never been.

00:39:12.409 --> 00:39:13.473
You will be.

00:39:58.088 --> 00:39:59.434
I'm taking you home.

00:40:01.905 --> 00:40:02.468
Sam!

00:40:13.554 --> 00:40:15.322
Sam! Here!

00:40:15.369 --> 00:40:16.511
You okay?

00:40:17.199 --> 00:40:18.075
I think.

00:40:18.670 --> 00:40:20.798
Can you move? Yeah. Help me.

00:41:22.177 --> 00:41:24.351
You've come home to us, mommy.

00:42:02.460 --> 00:42:04.431
So this is where she drowned her kids.

00:42:06.105 --> 00:42:07.576
That's why she could never go home.

00:42:09.367 --> 00:42:11.119
She was too scared to face them.

00:42:12.379 --> 00:42:13.959
You found her weak spot.

00:42:14.428 --> 00:42:15.711
Nice work, Sammy.

00:42:18.297 --> 00:42:20.441
I wish I could say the same for you.

00:42:20.566 --> 00:42:22.859
What were you thinking shooting
Casper in the face, you freak?

00:42:22.964 --> 00:42:25.468
Hey, saved your ass.

00:42:26.359 --> 00:42:29.379
I'll tell you another thing.
If you screwed up my car,

00:42:30.942 --> 00:42:32.162
I'll kill you.

00:42:44.735 --> 00:42:47.973
Okay, here's where dad went. It's
called Blackbottle Ridge, Colorado.

00:42:49.209 --> 00:42:50.977
Sounds charming. How far?

00:42:51.191 --> 00:42:53.052
About 600 miles.

00:42:53.756 --> 00:42:56.087
If we shag ass, we
can make it by morning.

00:42:57.976 --> 00:42:59.540
Dean, um...

00:43:02.122 --> 00:43:03.154
You're not going.

00:43:03.295 --> 00:43:05.720
The interview's in 10
hours. I got to be there.

00:43:10.536 --> 00:43:14.651
Yeah. Yeah, whatever.
I'll take you home.

00:43:35.244 --> 00:43:36.731
You'll call me if you find him?

00:43:39.739 --> 00:43:41.476
Maybe I can meet up with you later, huh?

00:43:41.773 --> 00:43:42.633
Yeah, all right.

00:43:46.635 --> 00:43:47.417
Sam.

00:43:51.485 --> 00:43:53.237
You know, we made a hell
of a team back there.

00:43:54.479 --> 00:43:55.073
Yeah.

00:44:14.328 --> 00:44:15.204
Jess!

00:44:17.082 --> 00:44:18.208
You home!?

00:45:00.347 --> 00:45:01.286
No!

00:45:04.232 --> 00:45:05.202
Sam!

00:45:05.233 --> 00:45:06.000
Jess!

00:45:07.752 --> 00:45:09.270
Sam! Sam!

00:45:10.521 --> 00:45:12.320
No! No!

00:45:13.237 --> 00:45:15.991
Jess! Jess! No!

00:46:01.992 --> 00:46:03.713
We got work to do.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
